01:49:35,023 --> 01:49:38,440
then your parents start to feel that we have a problem.

1838
01:49:38,520 --> 01:49:41,520
And then like you know how mothers are.

1839
01:49:42,840 --> 01:49:45,680
We say something, this and that, ten thousand things.

1840
01:49:45,760 --> 01:49:47,680
So I worry that.

1841
01:49:47,760 --> 01:49:50,680
Although I say things like, yes, go.

1842
01:49:50,760 --> 01:49:54,360
Absolutely, go. Enjoy life, she says like that.

1843
01:49:54,440 --> 01:49:57,560
But I know my mom, man, deep down, what will she think?

1844
01:49:57,640 --> 01:50:03,120
The second reason is that I was really aggressive last year when I left the studio.

1845
01:50:03,200 --> 01:50:06,360
And then in two or three months I started getting bored here.

1846
01:50:06,440 --> 01:50:08,440
So I was aggressively looking for a place.

1847
01:50:08,590 --> 01:50:10,510
that a place where I can live

1848
01:50:10,590 --> 01:50:16,590
and also like, so like for example, let's say if I get a three bedroom apartment

1849
01:50:17,520 --> 01:50:22,089
so one is a bedroom, the rest I can make different studios, like you know,

1850
01:50:22,169 --> 01:50:26,510
one place for podcast setup, one for Ask Anjeet sir setup, etc.

1851
01:50:26,590 --> 01:50:29,665
and I was aggressively looking for places.

1852
01:50:29,745 --> 01:50:34,590
If I like a place, the rent is so high, rent 3 lakhs, 3.5 lakhs.

1853
01:50:35,360 --> 01:50:39,360
Within Clifton's vicinity, like so you know our parents are like that.

1854
01:50:41,360 --> 01:50:47,280
Okay, when you're renting, the landlord is asking where your family is.

1855
01:50:47,360 --> 01:50:49,280
So the woman keeps coming and going.

1856
01:50:49,360 --> 01:50:51,280
So the rest of the time you'll be alone. Sorry.

1857
01:50:51,360 --> 01:50:53,280
I don't know what parties I have to throw.

1858
01:50:53,360 --> 01:50:56,280
Okay, one place I liked, it came with a rooftop.

1859
01:50:56,360 --> 01:51:00,910
And I really want a rooftop in my life because I never.

1860
01:51:00,990 --> 01:51:02,910
I never had a rooftop in my life.

1861
01:51:02,990 --> 01:51:04,910
There's no access in apartments.

1862
01:51:04,990 --> 01:51:06,990
There are only blue tanks.

1863
01:51:08,990 --> 01:51:10,910
So you know, there's a lot of air in Karachi.

1864
01:51:10,990 --> 01:51:12,910
I'm on the third floor.

1865
01:51:12,990 --> 01:51:14,990
And I kid you not, in the afternoon, there's no air.

1866
01:51:17,500 --> 01:51:20,420
I live next to the sea man. So imagine.

1867
01:51:20,500 --> 01:51:23,420
So you are on the roof with your friends. You can do so much.

1868
01:51:23,500 --> 01:51:28,420
So the roof was good, the house was good according to dimensions.

1869
01:51:28,500 --> 01:51:33,420
And I also need sunlight a lot. I need light.

1870
01:51:33,500 --> 01:51:40,420
I saw one in that, the whole floor is one apartment. Like the entire floor was one apartment.

1871
01:51:40,500 --> 01:51:45,500
But there is no light coming from anywhere. It was so badly made.

1872
01:51:46,040 --> 01:51:50,040
And one person refused to give it to the artist.

1873
01:51:51,040 --> 01:51:56,040
He asked me what I do. I said I am a YouTuber. He said no sir, we don't give it to the media.

1874
01:51:57,040 --> 01:51:58,040
I said why?

1875
01:51:59,040 --> 01:52:01,040
So he didn't say anything.

1876
01:52:02,040 --> 01:52:04,040
So he was a little religious.

1877
01:52:05,040 --> 01:52:07,960
So then I asked the state agent, he said, they do parties for the media.

1878
01:52:08,040 --> 01:52:09,960
I said, I am not that media guy.

1879
01:52:10,040 --> 01:52:12,210
Which party am I? I am a party myself.

1880
01:52:12,290 --> 01:52:20,210
Anyway, so many problems are there, so you don't get them for rental.

1881
01:52:20,290 --> 01:52:24,210
Big problems. It's a long way to buy an apartment of 6 million.

1882
01:52:24,290 --> 01:52:30,290
I was sending some links to Goglu. Karachi is so fucking over-hyped.

1883
01:52:30,720 --> 01:52:34,899
A street that is not built, a dirty street in Muhammad Ali society,

1884
01:52:34,979 --> 01:52:39,290
a house worth 7 million, a street that is not built, there are holes in it.

1885
01:52:39,840 --> 01:52:42,760
Damn it, why people choose to live like this?

1886
01:52:42,840 --> 01:52:43,760
Anyways.

1887
01:52:43,840 --> 01:52:49,760
So, and I find Karachi extremely over-hyped in terms of investing point.

1888
01:52:49,840 --> 01:52:51,760
I have zero investments in Karachi.

1889
01:52:51,840 --> 01:52:54,760
For primarily the same reason because there's no…

1890
01:52:54,840 --> 01:52:58,760
Your house, I saw a house, it was very beautiful.

1891
01:52:58,840 --> 01:53:03,760
Because you know I was looking for apartments so I joined a lot of these groups.

1892
01:53:03,840 --> 01:53:05,760
So the house was very beautiful.

1893
01:53:05,840 --> 01:53:06,910
It cost 40 crores.

1894
01:53:06,990 --> 01:53:11,410
Where in Phase 8, where there's no signal from the mobile, and no water and gas?

1895
01:53:11,490 --> 01:53:14,910
Why the fuck would you pay forty crores, man?

1896
01:53:14,990 --> 01:53:20,910
So yeah. So I totally get you, son. Sorry, I took the conversation from somewhere.

1897
01:53:20,990 --> 01:53:22,910
You need to step out of the house.

1898
01:53:22,990 --> 01:53:27,910
In the house, whatever it is, there's a house. There's no work vibe in the house.

1899
01:53:27,990 --> 01:53:32,990
And I don't understand work from home at all.

1900
01:53:33,740 --> 01:53:38,660
A man should step out for work. We are biologically wired to step out of the house and work.

1901
01:53:38,740 --> 01:53:41,360
When has it ever happened in history that a man is working from home?

1902
01:53:41,440 --> 01:53:46,860
So yes, it feels good to hear that this is the bed and this is me.

1903
01:53:46,940 --> 01:53:53,860
But no, man, there's no vibe. Get up, get ready, wear your shoes, start the car, start the bike, go somewhere.

1904
01:53:53,940 --> 01:53:57,660
So you feel like you're driven by purpose and that'll make you feel good.

1905
01:53:57,740 --> 01:54:00,790
And then of course there will be stressors, road stress, traffic.

1906
01:54:00,870 --> 01:54:02,790
It will be fine in its place.

1907
01:54:02,870 --> 01:54:05,790
But at the end of the day you'll feel you achieved something.

1908
01:54:05,870 --> 01:54:07,790
You don't achieve it sitting at home.

1909
01:54:07,870 --> 01:54:10,790
So that's primarily the reason why I'm super depressed.

1910
01:54:10,870 --> 01:54:13,790
It's because I'm like bound in this room.

1911
01:54:13,870 --> 01:54:16,790
Yeah man. Just fucking hating it.

1912
01:54:16,870 --> 01:54:19,790
It's a weird helplessness. I should have my own Asgandhi swag.

1913
01:54:19,870 --> 01:54:22,790
Someone make it. I'll send so many emails every week.

1914
01:54:22,870 --> 01:54:25,870
I have so many problems in my life. I swear to God.

1915
01:54:26,640 --> 01:54:27,190
So, yes,

1916
01:54:27,270 --> 01:54:34,040
you asked me to do university and you didn't tell me what you would do in university.

1917
01:54:34,120 --> 01:54:36,960
And what you will do outside, you didn't even tell me.

1918
01:54:37,040 --> 01:54:40,320
So I can't give you any advice in this.

1919
01:54:40,400 --> 01:54:46,040
That I do this plus co-working space. Yes, join the co-working space. It's good.

1920
01:54:46,120 --> 01:54:50,760
I also thought in between that I take some table somewhere.

1921
01:54:50,840 --> 01:54:53,910
Now the problem is when people.

1922
01:54:53,990 --> 01:54:59,910
When people know that you come here every day, they annoy you.

1923
01:54:59,990 --> 01:55:02,910
People don't let me be.

1924
01:55:02,990 --> 01:55:05,910
Again, I'm not complaining when people come and meet me. That's fine.

1925
01:55:08,920 --> 01:55:14,840
But don't make it a routine that we come everyday. We are not friends that we will sit everyday and have tea.

1926
01:55:14,920 --> 01:55:20,840
So I never joined the co-working space because I know the potential of our people.

1927
01:55:20,920 --> 01:55:24,840
Or they just don't let you be in your own space.

1928
01:55:24,920 --> 01:55:28,840
I am not there to mingle, I am here to do my work.

1929
01:55:28,920 --> 01:55:30,840
So this is my laptop, this is my table.

1930
01:55:30,920 --> 01:55:33,840
Yeah. So it becomes a big problem.

1931
01:55:33,920 --> 01:55:36,400
Anyways, so I would suggest you join.

1932
01:55:36,480 --> 01:55:38,400
Join some co working space

1933
01:55:38,480 --> 01:55:43,320
You will enjoy the process of getting there and getting things done

1934
01:55:43,400 --> 01:55:50,060
And even if your house is big, you said it's small and I didn't go into the issues of the sisters

1935
01:55:50,140 --> 01:55:55,820
I don't know what to say about this, I've never dealt with my sisters that way

1936
01:55:55,900 --> 01:56:00,520
So I don't know how to deal with women in that capacity

1937
01:56:00,600 --> 01:56:03,850
Honestly I don't have any memory either

1938
01:56:03,930 --> 01:56:07,730
I have lived with my family for 29 years

1939
01:56:07,810 --> 01:56:11,070
but I don't have any memories, we used to live in such a small house

1940
01:56:11,150 --> 01:56:16,230
I don't have any strong memories, I think it's like a brain's way to

1941
01:56:16,310 --> 01:56:19,590
you know, remove all the memories

1942
01:56:19,670 --> 01:56:25,870
So yeah, and the old memories are old, I don't live in nostalgia, I live in the present

1943
01:56:25,950 --> 01:56:29,390
Anyways, so yes, get into a space

1944
01:56:30,480 --> 01:56:37,875
And people who have been working from home, those who have gone from office to home,

1945
01:56:37,955 --> 01:56:41,400
what are your thoughts on it?

1946
01:56:41,480 --> 01:56:55,800
Or those who went from home due to COVID and then after a while they realized that's not the real deal and they were yearning for the world to open up so that they can step back into the office.

1947
01:56:55,880 --> 01:56:57,280
So this is definitely an experience.

1948
01:56:57,560 --> 01:56:58,493
share your card.

1949
01:56:58,573 --> 01:56:59,587
I wish you well.

1950
01:56:59,667 --> 01:57:00,220
Take care.

1951
01:57:00,300 --> 01:57:05,150
I really like your determination and your grit and if you have this kind of

1952
01:57:05,230 --> 01:57:10,910
kind of discipline in your life at 21, you're going to go very far in life, inshallah.

1953
01:57:10,990 --> 01:57:14,590
It's only a matter of sticking to your discipline.

1954
01:57:15,000 --> 01:57:20,600
and just making sure you don't slip out because you're young, you're making good money.

1955
01:57:20,680 --> 01:57:25,000
It's very easy to slip, but like be very, very firm.

1956
01:57:25,120 --> 01:57:28,120
and Insha Allah you'll do good in life. Thank you.

1957
01:57:28,990 --> 01:57:31,430
Someone has written very red fonts and sent them.

1958
01:57:31,510 --> 01:57:34,370
Please read this before coming to Canada.

1959
01:57:34,540 --> 01:57:38,899
Dear Junaid Bhai, okay, he said that he doesn't want to read red things,

1960
01:57:38,979 --> 01:57:41,356
so it's more than half of you, it's red.

1961
01:57:41,436 --> 01:57:42,960
So how will there be context?

1962
01:57:43,040 --> 01:57:46,320
Now you have mentioned four characters in this book.

1963
01:57:46,400 --> 01:57:50,320
Out of which one, two, three you have red-listed.

1964
01:57:50,400 --> 01:57:52,930
So if I don't read that, I will only read the fourth one.

1965
01:57:53,010 --> 01:57:53,310
How can I move forward after reading the fourth chapter?

1966
01:57:53,390 --> 01:57:54,930
I can't read the fourth page and move forward.

1967
01:57:55,010 --> 01:58:00,930
I can read it for you, but you, the audience, tell me what to do.

1968
01:58:01,010 --> 01:58:02,440
Kindly treat this message as anonymous.

1969
01:58:02,520 --> 01:58:05,960
I have written to you before, but this time I need to keep my name out of it.

1970
01:58:06,040 --> 01:58:10,040
You'll probably recognize me, but for this, let the anonymous voice float free.

1971
01:58:10,120 --> 01:58:11,030
Please don't mention any.

1972
01:58:11,110 --> 01:58:16,570
any identifier from my previous email. This one's personal. It's a rant, yes, but more

1973
01:58:16,650 --> 01:58:19,550
than that, it's a confession, a reflection, a cautionary tale.

1974
01:58:20,180 --> 01:58:24,980
stitched together from the silence between WhatsApp messages, fake smiles and empty brains.

1975
01:58:25,060 --> 01:58:30,580
Here are four characters and a crowd of extras from the play, That Is My Immigrant Life.

1976
01:58:30,660 --> 01:58:36,260
Each one come dressed as a family or friend, each one left wearing the mask of betrayal.

1977
01:58:45,660 --> 01:58:51,220
Second, about a woman in the family. Such a big paragraph, I can't read.

1978
01:58:51,300 --> 01:58:53,652
Third, about a friend.

1979
01:58:53,732 --> 01:58:57,608
Such a big paragraph, I can't read.

1980
01:58:57,688 --> 01:58:59,980
I can read the fourth.

1981
01:59:00,060 --> 01:59:01,360
Example four, the boys.

1982
01:59:01,440 --> 01:59:02,491
Still stuck in 2005.

1983
01:59:02,571 --> 01:59:07,061
I went to a university reunion hoping to find growth, new ideas, old brothers,

1984
01:59:07,141 --> 01:59:08,780
a spark of something evolved.

1985
01:59:08,860 --> 01:59:13,660
Instead, it was a walk back in the past. Same jokes, same bullying, same fragile masculinity.

1986
01:59:13,860 --> 01:59:18,660
You are not young, you are gay, why are your hair like this? Etc. etc.

1987
01:59:23,140 --> 01:59:27,440
No vision, no curiosity, only nostalgia marinated in insecurity.

1988
01:59:27,520 --> 01:59:32,160
In contrast, when I sit with Indians, they talk about stocks, entrepreneurship, ideas, and growth.

1989
01:59:32,240 --> 01:59:34,160
Then we ask why we are behind.

1990
01:59:34,240 --> 01:59:37,960
Example five, the leaders clout over community.

1991
01:59:38,040 --> 01:59:41,370
These are the worst ones, the self-declared community leaders.

1992
01:59:41,450 --> 01:59:45,671
always in suits, always in selfies, always in sing.

1993
01:59:45,751 --> 01:59:49,370
They host dawads with chandeliers and fake smiles.

1994
01:59:49,450 --> 01:59:53,370
Like each Facebook post is a campaign launch. Filtered faces, filtered friendships.

1995
01:59:53,450 --> 02:00:00,370
What more? They have zero intellect. Can't hold a decent conversation with you about any book or scientific theory.

1996
02:00:00,450 --> 02:00:02,370
Okay, I can't read the next one either.

1997
02:00:02,450 --> 02:00:07,450
But bring in a Pakistani celeb. They're first in line for the group photo. Then sometimes…

1998
02:00:08,010 --> 02:00:10,415
scam the artists out of the promised money.

1999
02:00:10,495 --> 02:00:14,859
They build cloud castles on shifting sand and dare to call themselves leaders.

2000
02:00:14,939 --> 02:00:18,959
They don't know a thing about struggles of Pakistanis here in Canada,

2001
02:00:19,039 --> 02:00:22,758
but they know everything, every angle of the camera.

2002
02:00:22,838 --> 02:00:26,834
So, Junaid Bhai, I write this not out of anger, but out of exhaustion.

2003
02:00:26,914 --> 02:00:28,760
Please be cautious when you come.

2004
02:00:28,840 --> 02:00:31,885
You will be welcomed with open arms and tight smiles.

2005
02:00:31,965 --> 02:00:34,250
There may even be a lavish dinner, but just

2006
02:00:34,330 --> 02:00:36,598
Just know many of those arms are hollow.

2007
02:00:36,678 --> 02:00:38,492
Many of those smiles are staged.

2008
02:00:38,572 --> 02:00:42,230
They don't represent the soul of our community, only its shadow.

2009
02:00:42,310 --> 02:00:48,770
They chase optics, not authenticity. They measure work in likes, not in legacy. Worth in likes.

2010
02:00:48,850 --> 02:00:53,494
And if in all this noise you have 10 minutes, I'd be honored to share a quiet handshake.

2011
02:00:53,574 --> 02:00:55,866
My story may not have the virality of others,

2012
02:00:55,946 --> 02:00:58,290
but it's stitched with struggle and sincerity.

2013
02:00:58,370 --> 02:01:01,220
Your voice has been in my ears in gyms or highways during-

2014
02:01:01,300 --> 02:01:03,553
during moments of both doubt and drive.

2015
02:01:03,633 --> 02:01:06,205
You've taught me more than most ever tried.

2016
02:01:06,285 --> 02:01:08,120
With respect, Anonymous."

2017
02:01:08,200 --> 02:01:13,614
I don't know man, I mean like thank you for nice words but when I couldn't read things,

2018
02:01:13,694 --> 02:01:15,620
maybe it was for me.

2019
02:01:15,700 --> 02:01:19,710
Okay, you've told me this, please read this before coming to Canada.

2020
02:01:19,790 --> 02:01:21,555
I'm not coming to Canada.

2021
02:01:21,635 --> 02:01:26,000
So one should never say never but like I'm just not too excited about.

2022
02:01:26,080 --> 02:01:27,600
about traveling at all.

2023
02:01:27,680 --> 02:01:31,200
I came back home from Budapest.

2024
02:01:31,280 --> 02:01:33,400
So, yeah.

2025
02:01:33,480 --> 02:01:35,400
Okay, you probably wrote it for me.

2026
02:01:35,480 --> 02:01:38,000
But now what should I do about your relatives?

2027
02:01:38,080 --> 02:01:39,400
About whom there are paragraphs.

2028
02:01:39,480 --> 02:01:41,400
Sorry, I couldn't understand the context.

2029
02:01:41,480 --> 02:01:42,600
But I understand.

2030
02:01:42,680 --> 02:01:47,600
Maybe, probably you meant for me that.

2031
02:01:47,680 --> 02:01:49,400
Okay, you have another email.

2032
02:01:49,480 --> 02:01:51,000
Now I am not reading both.

2033
02:01:51,080 --> 02:01:52,400
Others should also get a chance.

2034
02:01:52,480 --> 02:01:53,400
But yeah, thank you.

2035
02:01:53,480 --> 02:01:53,990
I don't know what to make of it.

2036
02:01:54,070 --> 02:01:56,030
But thank you so much for writing it.

2037
02:01:56,110 --> 02:01:59,710
Next one says a positive perspective from a Pakistani abroad.

2038
02:01:59,790 --> 02:02:04,870
I hope this email finds you well and in the best of health and spirits.

2039
02:02:04,950 --> 02:02:11,630
I've been following your series and truly appreciate the way you bring up important topics with honesty and humor.

2040
02:02:11,710 --> 02:02:12,510
One thing.

2041
02:02:12,590 --> 02:02:17,390
I just talked about Canada. Now I genuinely miss being in America.

2042
02:02:17,470 --> 02:02:20,190
There's like a particular sun.

2043
02:02:20,270 --> 02:02:21,640
The sun is different everywhere.

2044
02:02:21,720 --> 02:02:24,640
The sun is different in both the way of seeing and feeling.

2045
02:02:24,720 --> 02:02:27,640
The sun in America is very different.

2046
02:02:27,720 --> 02:02:29,640
Especially in Texas.

2047
02:02:29,720 --> 02:02:32,640
And I am missing the one in November.

2048
02:02:32,720 --> 02:02:36,640
Particularly Dallas. When the black ice falls.

2049
02:02:36,720 --> 02:02:40,640
I really miss being there. I have wonderful memories.

2050
02:02:40,720 --> 02:02:44,640
I met wonderful people over there.

2051
02:02:44,720 --> 02:02:46,720
It's been a while man. Need to come back.

2052
02:02:48,370 --> 02:02:55,408
I've noticed come up quite is the notion of Pakistani se door raho bahir or not trusting fellow Pakistanis abroad.

2053
02:02:55,488 --> 02:03:01,018
While I respect and acknowledge everyone's experiences, I wanted to humbly share my own,

2054
02:03:01,098 --> 02:03:03,070
which has been quite different.

2055
02:03:03,150 --> 02:03:08,296
I've been living abroad since 2017, first in Malaysia and now in Canada since 2019.

2056
02:03:08,376 --> 02:03:09,150
Alhamdulillah,

2057
02:03:09,230 --> 02:03:14,780
I've come across some genuinely kind-hearted and supportive people during this journey.

2058
02:03:14,900 --> 02:03:20,820
Before coming to Canada, I randomly searched on Facebook and found only one Pakistani student at my university.

2059
02:03:20,900 --> 02:03:30,403
I reached out to him and he went out of his way to help me from assisting with my university application to guiding me in finding my first job here.

2060
02:03:30,483 --> 02:03:32,600
Eventually he became my best friend.

2061
02:03:33,330 --> 02:03:36,431
I still remember one of my early days in Canada.

2062
02:03:36,511 --> 02:03:40,726
I didn't realize the last bus to my area on Sunday was at 6 p.m.

2063
02:03:40,806 --> 02:03:41,840
and I missed it.

2064
02:03:42,400 --> 02:03:44,128
I had no choice but to take a taxi.

2065
02:03:44,208 --> 02:03:46,553
The driver happened to be a Pakistani.

2066
02:03:46,633 --> 02:03:50,564
And when I told him I was new here and a student, he refused to take any fare,

2067
